error[E0458]: `f64` isn't declared here, so its `impl` can't hold `scale`
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/mixed_arithmetic/e0458.la:6:9
  |
6 |     fun scale(self, v: V): V = V { x: self * v.x };
  |         ^^^^^
  |
  = help: only `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div` and `rem` of the operator's shape (`fun mul(self, v: V): V`) can be added to a type you don't declare

error[E0458]: `f64 + i64` uses no type declared here, so it can't be defined here
  --> tests/programs/interfaces/mixed_arithmetic/e0458.la:7:9
  |
7 |     fun add(self, k: i64): f64 = self + (k as f64);
  |         ^^^
  |
  = help: arithmetic with a type you don't declare on the left goes in the module that declares the right-hand type, so each pair of types has one place that defines it

error[E0457]: this operand fits more than one `mul` with `V`: `i64`, `u8`
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/mixed_arithmetic/e0458.la:20:13
   |
20 |     let a = 2 * v;
   |             ^
   |
   = help: say which: `2 as i64` or `2 as u8`

error[E0403]: `f64 * V` gives V, but the place is f64
   --> tests/programs/interfaces/mixed_arithmetic/e0458.la:22:5
   |
22 |     k *= v;
   |     ^^^^^^
   |
   = help: keep it in a new variable: `let r = k * v;`

